Let $V$ be a complex projective threefold and let $\mathcal{L}$ be a linear system of positive dimension on $V$. Assume that a general member $S \in |\mathcal{L}|$ satisfies the following properties:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $S$ is irreducible;
\item for a resolution of singularities $\pi : \widetilde{S} \to S$, the geometric genus and irregularity vanish, i.e.\ $p_g(\widetilde{S}) = q(\widetilde{S}) = 0$;
\item $S$ is not a rational surface.
\end{enumerate}
The problem is to classify all such pairs $(V, \mathcal{L})$. In particular:
(a) produce a complete list of all known examples of pairs $(V, \mathcal{L})$ satisfying (1)–(3); and
(b) establish an upper bound on the dimension $\dim |\mathcal{L}|$ in terms of natural invariants of $V$ (or an absolute bound), under the above assumptions.

